  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1225 AM MST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nA weak shortwave will swing through the state today through early \nFriday, bringing low-end chances for precipitation across the higher \nterrain this evening through Friday morning. Have added PoPs up to \n25 percent above 7,500 feet in the central mountains as well as \nalong the MT Divide during the evening based on REFS guidance.\n\nDaytime temperatures will remain very stable and run within a few \ndegrees of normal through Friday with widespread highs ranging the \n40s. A ridge of high pressure will begin to amplify over the region \nFriday behind the departing shortwave, which will keep conditions \ndry and mild through late next week. Southerly flow will help warm \ntemperatures by more than 5 degrees on Sunday and temperatures will \ncontinue to run 5 to 10 degrees above climatological norms through \nmuch of next week, ranging the 50s for much of Southeast Idaho.",
